+# Quickwins: Cloud / Edge / IoT / HPC
+
+This patch provides practical artifacts and scripts to address the quick wins described in the platform review:
+
+Cloud
+- CI enforcement for cosign + Rekor (see .github/workflows/enforce_cosign_rekor.yml). Place COSIGN_PUB and REKOR_SERVER in GitHub Secrets.
+- Gatekeeper ConstraintTemplate requires resources to have annotation `mcp.provenance/signed=true` (k8s/gatekeeper/*).
+- NetworkPolicy sample and HPA example for Triton.
+- PrometheusRule sample for p95/p99 latency alerts.
+
+Edge
+- scripts/push_onnx_to_trt.py already present in repository; this patch adds helper to sign artifacts with KMS (scripts/sign_with_kms.sh) and a k3s install helper earlier.
+- RuntimeClass + PREEMPT_RT guidance already provided; use k8s/rt manifests from earlier patches.
+
+IoT
+- TPM attestation stub (iot/tpm_agent_stub.py) and mqtt_agent example exist; productionize with real TPM and secure provisioning.
+
+HPC
+- slurm/hpc_job_wrapper.sh: wrapper that runs distributed job, then uploads checkpoint and creates MCP record (scripts/upload_checkpoint_and_create_mcp.sh).
+
+How to use
+- Configure secrets: COSIGN_KMS_URI or COSIGN_PUB, REKOR_SERVER, S3_BUCKET, AEGIS_MCP_API, AWS creds.
+- Run CI enforcement to verify MCP provenance on PRs.
+- Use slurm wrapper to ensure checkpoints are ingested, signed and attached to MCP.
+- Deploy Gatekeeper and apply the ConstraintTemplate+Constraint to block deployments missing `mcp.provenance/signed=true`.
+
+Operator tasks
+- Provision KMS (AWS/GCP/Azure/HashiCorp) and use COSIGN KMS URIs for signing artifacts.
+- Deploy Gatekeeper (OPA) to the cluster and enable the ConstraintTemplate.
+- Install ExternalSecrets operator and configure SecretStore to fetch DB credentials from Vault.
+- Build and validate PREEMPT_RT node images for RT workloads; label nodes.
+
